meta {
  name: Voice sessions
  seq: 10
}

docs {
  # Voice sessions

  Run the requests in order. `00-login` stores `ACCESS_TOKEN`. Requests 01–02
  exercise one pipeline asset; requests 03–06 exercise a realtime draft and its
  published live version. Each settings request asserts the resolved engine mode
  and noise-cancellation mode before the matching session request creates the
  conversation and LiveKit room.

  Set these collection or environment variables before running:

  - `VOICE_FLOW_VERSION_ID`: a pipeline VoiceAgent flow version UUID.
  - `VOICE_MODE`: `test` for the draft or `live` for a published version
    (default `test` in the request).
  - `VOICE_REALTIME_DRAFT_FLOW_VERSION_ID`: the realtime draft flow version UUID.
  - `VOICE_REALTIME_LIVE_FLOW_VERSION_ID`: the realtime published version UUID
    (the same flow as the draft, after publishing).

  Join a returned room with the LiveKit console or CLI using its
  `VOICE_*_SERVER_URL`, `VOICE_*_CLIENT_TOKEN`, and `VOICE_*_ROOM_NAME`.
  Each token is a short-lived credential; do not commit it or copy it into
  shared notes. Enhanced noise-cancellation modes are rejected at publish, so
  the live asset must resolve `none` or `auto`.
}
